// PLL placement.  Only the PLLs have placement macros (the divider does not --
// evidence/desktop-vga-display.txt), and the open flow needs these three pins:
// without them nextpnr's free choice lands pll_nes inside a row-108 gap and the
// design has no violation-free placement at all -- an eight-seed sweep found
// none, and two seeds did not even route (`Net hclk5 has no route to the FCLK
// of u_hdmi.hdmi.serializer.gwSer0`).  With pll_nes at PLL_R[0], the site
// nearest the logic, seeds 17 and 19 measured setup 0 / hold 0 on the nestang
// netlist; on the cleaned TinyTang netlist seeds 1-32 at PLL_R[0] all failed.
//
// pll_nes is at PLL_R[0].  It sat at PLL_L[0] from 2026-10-11 because seeds
// 1-32 there failed setup or hold on the cleaned TinyTang netlist, and seed 2
// at PLL_L[0] passed; PLL_L[0] is also the one site whose CLKOUT0 has a
// modelled clock wire (`TLPLL0CLK0`), and routing `clk` onto it gives a
// timing-clean core that is dead on the board -- the chipdb's TLPLL0CLK0 ->
// spine -> bridge path is wrong somewhere.  What kept this core working was
// the stock router refusing that hop; the fork no longer refuses it, so the
// PLL_L[0] build now comes out with `clk` on global resources only.  Moving
// the HDMI PLLs beside the right-side serialisers removed the timing failure
// that held PLL_R[0] back (seeds 1-4 pass setup and hold), and PLL_R[0]'s own
// wire `TRPLL0CLK0` is the one this project has measured good (TinyNES
// core-reference DEV-009).  See core-log entry 52.
//
// Put the HDMI PLLs beside the right-side TMDS serializers.  With pll_hdmi at
// PLL_L[3], its 371.25 MHz output crossed the die on general routing and the
// desktop picture failed when the FPGA was hot.  TinyNES's PLL_R[3] route
// shortened that path; its 27 MHz reference PLL is on the same side.
// pll_nes moves with them, to PLL_R[0], for the clock-wire reason above.
//
// Instance names are the flattened cell names nextpnr reports.
INS_LOC "pll_27.PLL_inst"   PLL_R[1];
INS_LOC "pll_hdmi.PLL_inst" PLL_R[3];
INS_LOC "pll_nes.PLL_inst"  PLL_R[0];
// The divider must use the HCLK block that serves the HDMI OSER10s.
INS_LOC "div5" RIGHTSIDE[4];
